--- 1. Dependency map discovered by reading analysis/*.py (before running anything) ---

v8 canon (analysis_out_v6) provenance, reconstructed:
  * DEM source of v6 = maps/full_surface_and_subsurface_merged.pcd (NOT aerial_crop.pcd):
    the v6 cache is named dem_grid_full_surface_and_subsurface_merged.npz, which run_roof
    only produces when ROOF_DEM_PCD is set to that file. Grid: (641,764) x-major z[ix,iy],
    xmin 1200.7194, ymin 500.1730, res 0.5 (local frame, origin 479158/7089826).
    merged surface vs aerial_crop co-registration: median 0.00 m, std 0.04 m
    (analysis_out/merged_dem_validate.json). aerial_crop bbox x 1299.11-1598.40,
    y 409.98-721.56 (25.6M pts); merged bbox x 1200.72-1520.72, y 500.17-881.67.
  * Tube basis of v6 = FAST-LIO first flight chained into Ed's slice frame:
    maps/flf_30cm_ed.pcd (skeleton), maps/flf_10cm_ed.pcd (sections, roof ghost screen).
  * Exact v8 command sequence is not recorded verbatim (rerun_arcfix.log holds only the
    stdout); reconstructed from PROGRESS.md 2026-08-13/14 + setup_ed_frame.py docstring.

Script -> inputs (env var, default) -> outputs
  run_morphometry.py   ANALYSIS_OUT(analysis_out); MORPHO_SKEL_PCD(maps/tube_30cm_aerial.pcd);
                       MORPHO_SECT_PCD(maps/tube_10cm_aerial.pcd); reads/writes
                       OUT/skeleton_poly.npz cache (L1 skeleton, RNG seed 7, grid decimation
                       floor(Q/2 m) -> NOT exactly translation-invariant: a z shift changes
                       the grid phase of the initial samples); writes centreline.csv,
                       morphometry.csv, morphometry_summary.json, fig_skeleton_*.png,
                       fig_sections_gallery.png. Flip rule uses sky_y=640 (xy only).
  run_roof.py          ANALYSIS_OUT; ROOF_DEM_PCD(maps/aerial_crop.pcd) -> cache
                       OUT/dem_grid_<stem>.npz (per-cell max 0.5 m, 3x3 median, grid origin =
                       cloud min corner); ROOF_TUBE_PCD(maps/tube_10cm_aerial.pcd);
                       reads OUT/morphometry.csv, OUT/aerial_holes.json (centroid xy +
                       semi_major only), OUT/uncertainty_budget.json (sigma_tau);
                       writes roof_thickness.csv, roof_summary.json, fig_roof_*.png.
  validate_ed_registration.py  ANALYSIS_OUT(analysis_out_ed); VALID_TUBE_PCD(maps/tube_10cm_ed.pcd);
                       HARDCODED maps/aerial_10cm.pcd (ellipsoidal!) near S3;
                       HARDCODED analysis_out/aerial_holes.json (S3 xy only) and
                       analysis_out/transform_flf_ed_chain.json (two-SLAM zones, datum-free);
                       reads OUT/registration_report.json (rim rms), OUT/roof_thickness.csv,
                       OUT/uncertainty_budget.json; writes OUT/registration_validation.json and
                       updates OUT/uncertainty_budget.json (sigma_reg, sigma_tau).
                       -> needs an env override for the aerial cloud (VALID_AERIAL_PCD).
  run_planetary.py     ANALYSIS_OUT; reads OUT/roof_summary.json, morphometry_summary.json,
                       planetary_catalogue.csv; writes planetary_summary.json. Datum-free.
  chain_flf_to_ed.py / chain_slf_to_ed.py   HARDCODED analysis_out/ (transform_ed_slice.json,
                       flf/slf_transform_landmark.json, centreline.csv) and maps/tube_30cm.pcd,
                       flf_30cm.pcd, slf_30cm.pcd (SLAM frames). GICP between SLAM-frame maps:
                       independent of the surface datum. Write maps/flf_*_ed.pcd,
                       maps/slf_*_ed.pcd, analysis_out/transform_*_ed_chain.json;
                       chain_slf_to_ed additionally writes analysis_out_v6/flight2_repeatability.json
                       (HARDCODED OUT6) from OUT6/centreline.csv + maps/flf_30cm_ed.pcd.
                       -> NOT rerun for v9 (would rewrite the v8-canon maps and the chain does
                       not depend on the datum); the ortho maps are the existing ed maps plus
                       the measured translation. flight2_repeatability for v9 is recomputed
                       from the existing chain transform (new SLF_CHAIN_REUSE=1 path, no GICP).
  compare_bases.py     HARDCODED A=analysis_out_ed, B=analysis_out_v6; writes B/basis_comparison.json.
                       -> B made env-selectable (ANALYSIS_OUT), A stays analysis_out_ed
                       (ellipsoidal): dceil will differ from v6 by exactly dz, dtau must not.
  orbital_dem_test.py  ANALYSIS_OUT(analysis_out_v6); HARDCODED cache name
                       dem_grid_full_surface_and_subsurface_merged.npz; reads roof_thickness.csv;
                       writes orbital_dem_test.json, fig_orbital_dem_test.png.
                       -> cache name derived from ROOF_DEM_PCD (default unchanged).
  national_dem_check.py ANALYSIS_OUT(analysis_out_v6); same HARDCODED cache name; reads
                       maps/national_dem_site.tif (ArcticDEM, EPSG:3413, ellipsoidal) and
                       maps/islandsdem10m_site.tif (EPSG:3057, orthometric); writes
                       national_dem_check.json, fig_national_dem_check.png.
  run_review_stats.py  ANALYSIS_OUT(analysis_out_ed); reads OUT/roof_thickness.csv,
                       uncertainty_budget.json, planetary_catalogue.csv, morphometry_summary.json,
                       morphometry.csv, aerial_holes.json; HARDCODED analysis_out/tube_holes.json,
                       flf_tube_holes.json (SLAM frame, datum-free); writes review_stats.json.
                       Absolute-z fields: terrain.net_centreline.start/end (z_ceil).
  collect_paper_numbers.py ANALYSIS_OUT; reads registration_report.json, uncertainty_budget.json,
                       morphometry_summary.json, roof_summary.json, planetary_summary.json,
                       vertical_check.json, review_stats.json, registration_validation.json,
                       roof_thickness.csv; writes paper_numbers.json. Provenance note keyed on
                       OUT.name.endswith("_v6") and hardcodes the DEM file name.
  setup_ed_frame.py    seeds an ANALYSIS_OUT dir with aerial_holes.json, tube_holes.json,
                       vertical_check.json, planetary_catalogue.csv, dem cache,
                       uncertainty_budget.json, registration_report.json from analysis_out/.
                       For v9 the seed is done by a new script (seed_v9_ortho.py) that copies
                       these from analysis_out_v6 and z-shifts the absolute-z fields
                       (aerial hole centroid z, vertical_check q*_aerial/q*_tube, registration_report
                       aerial_holes centroid z). tube_holes.json is SLAM-frame: unchanged.
Figure scripts:
  make_figures.py      ANALYSIS_OUT; FIGS HARDCODED to the manuscript figures dir; reads
                       roof_thickness.csv, morphometry.csv, centreline.csv, planetary_catalogue.csv,
                       aerial_holes.json, review_stats.json, orbital_dem_test.json.
                       Absolute-z axis: morphometry panel g "centreline z (m)".
  make_ed_figures.py   ANALYSIS_OUT; EDFIG_SHELL_PCD(flf_30cm_aerial), EDFIG_SECT_PCD(flf_10cm_aerial);
                       HARDCODED maps/aerial_10cm.pcd (panel b), analysis_out/roof_thickness.csv
                       (4-DOF baseline ceiling, ellipsoidal, panel c), analysis_out/
                       transform_ed_slice.json + transform_flf_ed_chain.json + aerial_holes.json;
                       absolute-z axes: registration panel c, consistency panel a, centreline panel b.
  make_dem_validation_figure.py ANALYSIS_OUT(v6); FIGS hardcoded; imports orbital_dem_test
                       (same cache name); reads national_dem_check.json, maps/national_dem_site.tif,
                       roof_thickness.csv.
  render_merged_showcase.py  ANALYSIS_OUT; SHOWCASE_TUBE_PCD(flf_10cm_aerial); HARDCODED
                       maps/merged_surface_10cm.pcd (ellipsoidal) + cache name; reads
                       centreline.csv, aerial_holes.json; writes OUT/renders/showcase_*.png.
  make_merged_showcase_figure.py ANALYSIS_OUT; SHOWCASE_TUBE_PCD; HARDCODED
                       maps/merged_surface_10cm.pcd, cache name, FIGS; panel c has HARDCODED
                       absolute-elevation text anchors (229.5, 242.5/248.5, 238.5/246.5) in the
                       ellipsoidal range; ylabels "elevation (m, local)".
  render_skeleton_3d.py ANALYSIS_OUT; SKEL3D_TUBE_PCD; FIGS hardcoded (writes skeleton_3d.png
                       straight into the manuscript dir!) -> FIGS env needed.

v9 input plan:
  surface: new LAZ (EPSG:8088, orthometric ISH2004) -> pyproj EPSG:8088->EPSG:32627
           ("Inverse of Iceland Lambert 2016 + ISN2016 to WGS 84 (1) + UTM zone 27N";
           the ISN2016->WGS84 (1) step is a null transformation, pipeline has no helmert
           step; pyproj-stated accuracy 1.0 m), minus origin (479158, 7089826), z untouched.
           maps/aerial_isn16_ortho_crop.pcd  (aerial_crop bbox, full res)  -> old/new comparison
           maps/aerial_isn16_ortho_dem.pcd   (merged-cloud bbox, full res) -> ROOF_DEM_PCD
           maps/aerial_isn16_ortho_10cm.pcd  (union bbox, 10 cm voxel)     -> validate/ED fig b
           maps/aerial_isn16_ortho_surface_10cm.pcd (merged bbox crop of the 10 cm) -> showcase
  tube:    maps/{flf,slf,tube}_{10,30}cm_ed_ortho.pcd = ed maps + (0,0,dz) if the rule passes.
